<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">630 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">630 CE in world history: 12 events, 2 births and 1 death. 252 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/626">626 CE</a><a href="/years/627">627 CE</a><a href="/years/628">628 CE</a><a href="/years/629">629 CE</a><a href="/years/630" aria-current="page">630 CE</a><a href="/years/632">632 CE</a><a href="/years/633">633 CE</a><a href="/years/634">634 CE</a><a href="/years/636">636 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-11">11 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Muhammad enters Mecca and clears the Kaaba of idols</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By the usual reckoning, Muhammad and some 10,000 followers took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> with little bloodshed. The idols around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a> were destroyed and it was rededicated as the centre of Islamic worship.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/true-cross" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/true-cross.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-21">21 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Heraclius restores the True Cross to Jerusalem</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition on this day, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> returned the relic of the cross, captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> in 614, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. Within a decade the city fell to the Arab armies.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/true-cross">True Cross</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-27">27 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Shahrbaraz usurps the Sasanian throne from Ardashir III</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz">Shahrbaraz</a>, a leading Sasanian general under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> who had captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in 614, usurped the throne from Ardashir III. He was killed by Iranian nobles six weeks later, in the turmoil that preceded the Arab conquest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz">Shahrbaraz</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/tang-campaign-against-the-eastern-turks">Tang campaign against the Eastern Turks</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Tang campaign against the Eastern Turks was a military expedition launched by Emperor Taizong that defeated the Eastern Turkic Khaganate in 630 CE.</p></div></li></ol></section>
